---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BEEHIIV_EMBED_URL, BEEHIIV_FORM_ID } from '../../site.config.mjs';
import { LIMITS, LAST_CHECKED } from '../lib/rules-data';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
import history from '../../data/rules-history.json';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { FAQS } from '../lib/faqs';
import { GUIDES } from '../lib/guides';
const latest = (history.entries as { date: string; title: string; summary: string }[])[0];
---
<Base title="ChatGPT Plugin Submission Checklist & Grader | PluginLint" description="Free, private tools for a ChatGPT plugin submission: checklist, listing grader, MCP tool-output privacy auditor, test-case linter and sourced rules.">
  <h1>Get your ChatGPT plugin listing right the first time</h1>
  <p class="lede">PluginLint is a free toolkit for developers submitting a plugin to the ChatGPT plugin directory. Check your listing fields against OpenAI’s published limits before the submission portal rejects them.</p>
  <p class="answer"><strong>In short:</strong> a ChatGPT directory plugin’s display name and short description must each be one line of at most {LIMITS.displayName} characters, the long description at most {LIMITS.longDescription.toLocaleString('en-US')}, and you can add up to {LIMITS.starterPromptsMax} starter prompts. Plugins with a remote MCP server also need exactly five positive and three negative test cases and explicit tool annotations. PluginLint checks these in your browser before you submit.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href={u('/grader/')}>Open the listing grader</a> <a class="btn secondary" href={u('/rules/')}>See all the limits</a></p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Listing grader</h3>
    <p>Paste your display name, subtitle, description, starter prompts, capabilities, URLs and brand colours. You get a score and a pass / warn / fail list with a plain-language fix for each issue. It runs entirely in your browser; nothing is uploaded.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Tool-output privacy auditor</h3>
    <p>Paste real MCP tool results. It flags personal data, session/trace/request IDs, timestamps, internal account IDs, secrets, debug payloads and upsell text — the things OpenAI’s review page asks you to remove — and checks which ones your privacy policy mentions. <a href={u('/tools/tool-output-privacy-audit/')}>Open the auditor</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Test-case linter</h3>
    <p>Paste your <code>tools/list</code> result and draft test cases. It checks the five-positive / three-negative rule, tool names and annotations, then writes a <code>chatgpt-app-submission.json</code> that validates against OpenAI’s public schema. <a href={u('/tools/test-case-linter/')}>Open the linter</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Rules reference + change log</h3>
    <p>Every final-submission limit in one table, linked to the OpenAI page it comes from. A small script re-reads those two public docs pages once a day and records any wording change, so you can see when a limit moves.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Plain-English guides</h3>
    <ul>
      {GUIDES.map((g) => <li><a href={u(`/guides/${g.slug}/`)}>{g.title}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="checklist">ChatGPT plugin submission checklist</h2>
  <p>What final directory submission checks, per OpenAI’s <a href="https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission-errors" rel="noopener">submission-errors reference</a>. Items marked “remote MCP” apply only to plugins with a remote MCP server.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Listing fields within the final limits below — check them with the <a href={u('/grader/')}>listing grader</a>.</li>
    <li>A category from the supported list and a semantic version; a new release needs a new version (<a href={u('/rules/')}>all rules</a>).</li>
    <li>Passing safety and security scans for every bundled skill (can take up to 2 hours).</li>
    <li>A verified developer or business identity and all required policy attestations.</li>
    <li>Remote MCP: HTTPS website, support, privacy policy and terms URLs, and a demo-recording URL.</li>
    <li>Remote MCP: exactly five positive and three negative test cases plus release notes — <a href={u('/tools/test-case-linter/')}>lint them</a> (<a href={u('/guides/mcp-test-cases/')}>guide</a>).</li>
    <li>Remote MCP: a production HTTPS MCP server URL, a completed domain-verification challenge and a current tool scan.</li>
    <li>Remote MCP: explicit <code>readOnlyHint</code>, <code>openWorldHint</code> and <code>destructiveHint</code> on every tool (<a href={u('/guides/mcp-tool-annotations/')}>annotations explained</a>).</li>
    <li>Remote MCP: reviewer-ready demo credentials when the server uses OAuth, and screenshots only if the server provides custom UI (<a href={u('/guides/screenshot-size-requirements/')}>sizes</a>).</li>
    <li>Tool outputs that return only what the request needs — <a href={u('/tools/tool-output-privacy-audit/')}>audit them</a> (<a href={u('/guides/undisclosed-data-types-rejection/')}>why</a>).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Then read <a href={u('/guides/why-chatgpt-plugin-submissions-get-rejected/')}>why ChatGPT plugin submissions get rejected</a> for the review-stage causes.</p>
  <p class="meta">Want a human check? An optional paid <a href={u('/review/')}>submission review</a> is available; the tools above stay free.</p>

  <h2>The limits people hit most</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Field</th><th>Final-submission limit</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Display name</td><td>{LIMITS.displayName} characters, one line</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Short description (subtitle)</td><td>{LIMITS.subtitle} characters, one line</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Long description</td><td>{LIMITS.longDescription.toLocaleString('en-US')} characters</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Starter prompts</td><td>Up to {LIMITS.starterPromptsMax}, each ≤ {LIMITS.starterPrompt} characters, unique, no @mentions</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Capabilities</td><td>Up to {LIMITS.capabilitiesMax}, each ≤ {LIMITS.capability} characters</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p class="meta">Last checked against OpenAI’s docs on {LAST_CHECKED}.{latest && <> Latest watcher entry: {latest.date} — {latest.summary}</>}</p>

  <h2 id="newsletter">Get an email when the rules change</h2>
  {BEEHIIV_FORM_ID ? (
    <div>
      <iframe src={`https://subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com/v3/forms/${BEEHIIV_FORM_ID}`} title="Newsletter sign-up" width="100%" height="330" frameborder="0" scrolling="no" style="border:0;max-width:100%;width:100%" loading="lazy"></iframe>
      <noscript><p><a href={BEEHIIV_EMBED_URL}>Subscribe on beehiiv</a></p></noscript>
      <p class="meta">Prefer a page? <a href={BEEHIIV_EMBED_URL} rel="noopener">Subscribe on beehiiv</a>. One email when the rules change, unsubscribe any time.</p>
    </div>
  ) : (
    <div class="todo">
      <p><strong>TODO (site owner):</strong> newsletter sign-up goes here. Set <code>BEEHIIV_FORM_ID</code> in <code>site.config.mjs</code>. Until then no sign-up form is shown and no email is collected.</p>
    </div>
  )}

  <Faq faqs={FAQS.home} />

  <h2>Who runs this?</h2>
  <p>An independent developer. PluginLint is not affiliated with OpenAI. It uses only OpenAI’s public developer documentation as its source and does not collect or scrape data from chatgpt.com. <a href={u('/about/')}>More about the project</a>.</p>
</Base>
